From fe7204b80218d0ff23abec498dc7704fc5ebe454 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jonnyczi <czijonny@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:16:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Finish the restored extras state in rebuild_image.py

track_extra_functions.py --restore writes the extras' rows only. rebuild_image.py
rebuilt each extra's object and stopped there, so a fresh checkout's state had no
objects, no registry_c and no registry file. cross_build.populations() reads
state["objects"], so perf_f80.py build and android_game.py compile stop with a
KeyError; release_build.py and arm64_link.py read it with .get and link no
extras at all.

The rejection pass, the registry and the object list that end lift_extra.py's
main are now lift_extra.finalize, which main and rebuild_image.py both call.
main's behaviour is unchanged. The stamp tests' fixture now holds the arm work
list and the module ranges itself, so the tests give the same result on a
fresh clone as on a checkout with a map build.
